<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 30 0 R/Alt(Line plot comparing three impurity criteria, Gini, entropy and classification error (CE), against probability from 0 to 1. All three curves are symmetric around p = 0.5, are 0 at p = 0 and p = 1, and peak at p = 0.5. Entropy, a red curve, is the highest, peaking at about 0.69. Gini, a blue curve, peaks at 0.5. CE is a green inverted V made of two straight lines that also peaks at 0.5, touching the Gini curve there and lying below it everywhere else.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block/BBox[72.85714 174.31543 422.57144 493.04236]>>]/K[21]/Pg 234 0 R>>
